# PART 4 — MATCHER: DATING DISCOVERY

## 6. Core functionality

Create a Tinder-style swipe discovery experience.

Display one student profile at a time.

Each profile card must show:

- Profile picture.
- Username.
- Bio.
- Institute.
- Year.

The profile picture should occupy most of the card.

Include:
- Swipe right to like.
- Swipe left to pass.
- On-screen like button.
- On-screen pass button.
- Tap profile to view additional details if available.

Support:
- Touch gestures on mobile.
- Mouse gestures or buttons on desktop.
- Smooth animations.
- Haptic feedback where supported.

## 7. Dating discovery logic

All registered and eligible users should be included in the discovery pool.

Rules:

- Never show the currently logged-in user's own profile.
- Never show suspended or deleted accounts.
- Never show blocked users.
- Never show users who have blocked the current user.
- Do not repeatedly show profiles already passed or liked.
- Do not display the same profile multiple times in the active queue.
- Do not show someone again after a mutual match.
- Prevent duplicate likes.
- Prevent users from liking themselves.
- Handle simultaneous likes safely.

For the first version, use a randomised discovery feed.

Do not introduce complicated recommendation algorithms.

## 8. Like and pass logic

When a user swipes right:
- Record a like in the database.
- Check whether the other person has already liked the current user.
- If yes, create a mutual match.
- If no, save the like and continue.

When a user swipes left:
- Record a pass.
- Do not create a match.
- Exclude the passed profile from subsequent discovery sessions.

All operations must be protected against duplicate submissions and network retries.

## 9. Mutual matching

When two users like each other:

1. Create a unique mutual match record.
2. Notify both users.
3. Display a celebratory match screen.
4. Reveal their Instagram usernames to each other.
5. Provide an "Open Instagram" button.

The Instagram profile URL should be generated using the voluntarily supplied username:

https://www.instagram.com/USERNAME/

Do not implement an in-app messaging system.

Do not reveal Instagram usernames to users who have not mutually matched.

Provide a "Report" and "Unmatch" option.

Unmatching must prevent further discovery or interactions between the two accounts unless the user explicitly resets that relationship.

## 10. Empty discovery state

If the user has viewed all eligible profiles, display:

"You're all caught up!"

Include:
- A friendly illustration or minimal graphic.
- Explanation that more profiles will appear when new students join.
- A refresh button to check for newly registered users.

Refreshing must not reset previously recorded likes and passes.

Do not show an infinite spinner or repeatedly load already rejected profiles.

