# PART 15 — EDGE CASES

## 32. Dating edge cases

Test all of the following:

1. User tries to like themselves.
2. User likes someone who has already liked them.
3. Two users like each other simultaneously.
4. User repeatedly clicks the Like button.
5. User loses internet connection while liking.
6. User refreshes immediately after a match.
7. User logs in from another device.
8. User deletes their account after matching.
9. User blocks an existing match.
10. User unmatches someone.
11. User has no remaining profiles.
12. A new student joins after the user exhausts the feed.
13. A profile becomes suspended while appearing in the swipe queue.
14. A user changes their username.
15. A user changes their profile photograph.

## 33. Matchmaking edge cases

Test:

1. User nominates themselves.
2. User selects the same person twice.
3. Two users nominate the same pair in reverse order.
4. A nominated student deletes their account.
5. A nominated student is suspended.
6. A nominated student has not registered.
7. A nomination is withdrawn.
8. A nomination is reported.
9. A user submits multiple nominations rapidly.
10. A nominated person refuses public participation.

## 34. Voting edge cases

Test:

1. A user votes YES twice.
2. A user votes NO twice.
3. A user tries to change a vote.
4. A pairing is removed during voting.
5. One participant withdraws consent.
6. A voter deletes their account.
7. A voter is suspended.
8. Two users vote simultaneously.
9. A pairing receives zero votes.
10. A pairing has only one vote.
11. Two pairings have identical scores.
12. A pairing has an unusually high approval percentage but very few votes.

## 35. Authentication and profile edge cases

Test:

1. Google authentication fails.
2. User cancels Google login.
3. User closes the browser during registration.
4. Username is already taken.
5. Username contains invalid characters.
6. Profile picture upload fails.
7. User submits an empty bio.
8. User skips mandatory institute selection.
9. User skips year selection.
10. User tries to access the dashboard without completing their profile.
11. User tries to access /admin without permission.
12. User changes devices.
13. User logs out.
14. User deletes their account.

Every edge case should have a sensible response and must not corrupt the database.

